nts are extremely sparse.** In the window, node 1010 has only 2 events (2 partners) and 883 only 3 events (all inbound) [step_02].\n\n**1010 has exactly one outbound route:** 1010 \u2192 66 [step_03]. That single outbound event does *not* fall in [58518, 60917] [step_15], so combined with the temporal binning [step_13] it must occur late, in [68118, 70517].\n\n**883's inbound \"last hops\"** are only 729, 1038, 1209 [step_04], and their arrival times are: one in [63318,65717] (strictly *before* 1010 ever emits, so unusable), and two in [70518,75317] [step_14].\n\n**The frontier does not meet.** 66's out-neighbourhood is {31, 499, 1688, 1824, 1952} [step_06]. The in-neighbourhoods of 883's three feeders are {1090,1600} [step_11], {1951} [step_10], {149,296,459,582,990,1542} [step_09] \u2014 disjoint from 66's out-set. So any route is \u22655 directed hops (1010\u219266\u2192?\u2192?\u2192feeder\u2192883), all of which would have to fire inside roughly 70517\u219272917 with \u2264600-unit gaps.\n\n**Confounder controls.** The static k-hop hull around 1010 is large and does contain 1209 [step_05], and 66 touches genuine hubs (1688: 160 events/132 partners; 1824: 65 events) [step_12]. Local activity is dense in the relevant band [step_16]. That means an *order-ignoring* connection and plenty of ambient volume exist \u2014 but neither is evidence of a cascade, and the directed frontiers still fail to intersect within the required latency budget.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_78b94701\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883, 66, 729, 1038, 1209],\n  \"window\": [51317, 89717],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"narrative\": \"Node 1010 emits exactly one outbound event in the window (1010->66), and it occurs late, in [68118,70517] (ruled out of the earlier bin by step_15). Node 883 is purely a receiver with three inbound events; one arrives before 1010 emits anything and the other two arrive in [70518,75317]. The forward frontier from 1010 after one hop is {31,499,1688,1824,1952}, while the backward frontier into 883 after two hops is {1090,1600,1951,149,296,459,582,990,1542}; these sets are disjoint, so any candidate route needs five or more directed hops that would all have to fire in strict order with <=600-unit gaps inside a ~2400-unit slot. No such chain is evidenced. The static 3-hop hull does connect 1010's neighbourhood to 1209 (a feeder of 883) and 66 touches high-degree hubs 1688/1824, but those are order-free/popularity artefacts, not time-respecting influence.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 40256, "total_output_tokens": 7244, "total_tokens": 47500, "total_latency_ms": 98856, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}